  "readme_excerpt": "# LumiTrace \ud83c\udf1f **Temporal Low-Light Video Restoration using Illumination-Guided Transformers** Transform dark, noisy video footage into clear, vibrant scenes while maintaining temporal consistency and eliminating flicker artifacts. [![HuggingFace Model](https://img.shields.io/badge/\ud83e\udd17-Model%20on%20HuggingFace-blue)](https://huggingface.co/rajtiwariee/lumitrace) [![License](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-Apache%202.0-green.svg)](LICENSE) ## \ud83c\udfaf Project Overview LumiTrace extends the state-of-the-art [Retinexformer](https://github.com/caiyuanhao1998/Retinexformer) (ICCV 2023) architecture with temporal consistency mechanisms to enable professional-grade low-light video enhancement. **Key Features**: - \ud83d\udd25 Built on Retinexformer (2nd place NTIRE 2024 Challenge) - \u26a1 PyTorch 2.x with mixed-precision training - \ud83c\udfac Temporal consistency for flicker-free videos - \ud83d\udcca Trained on LOL-v1 & LOL-v2 datasets - \ud83d\ude80 Production-ready inference pipeline - \ud83e\udd17 Published on HuggingFace Hub ## \ud83d\udcca Results ### LOL-v1 Performance | Metric | Stage 1 | Stage 2 | |--------|---------|---------| | PSNR | 22.09 dB | **22.70 dB** | | SSIM | 0.8150 | **0.8389** | ### LOL-v2-Real Performance | Metric | Stage 1 | Stage 2 | |--------|---------|---------| | PSNR | 21.72 dB | **21.72 dB** | | SSIM | 0.7925 | **0.8199** | ### Visual Examples **Image Comparisons:** <div align=\"center\"> <img src=\"samples/compare_111.png\" width=\"48%\" alt=\"Comparison 1: Low-light input (left) vs Enhanced output (right)\" /> <img src=\"samples/compare_55.png\" width=\"48%\" alt=\"Comparison 2: Low-light input (left) vs Enhanced output (right)\" /> </div> <div align=\"center\"> <img src=\"samples/compare_547.png\" width=\"48%\" alt=\"Comparison 3: Low-light input (left) vs Enhanced output (right)\" /> <img src=\"samples/compare_79.png\" width=\"48%\" alt=\"Comparison 4: Low-light input (left) vs Enhanced output (right)\" /> </div> **Video Enhancement Demo:** <div align=\"center\"> <table> <tr> <td align=\"center\"><b>Input (Low-Light)</b></td> <td align=\"center\"><b>LumiTrace Enhanced</b></td> </tr> <tr> <td><img src=\"samples/demo2_test_file.gif\" width=\"100%\" alt=\"Low-light input video\" /></td> <td><img src=\"samples/demo2.gif\" width=\"100%\" alt=\"Enhanced output video\" /></td> </tr> </table> </div> *Demonstrates temporal consistency and flickering reduction in real-world low-light video* ## \ud83d\ude80 Quick Start ### Installation ```bash # Clone repository git clone https://github.com/yourusername/LumiTrace cd LumiTrace # Setup environment ./scripts/setup_env.sh # Or use cloud setup ./scripts/setup_cloud.sh # For CUDA environments ``` ### Download Pre-trained Model **Option 1: From HuggingFace (Recommended)** ```bash # Download via Python from huggingface_hub import hf_hub_download checkpoint = hf_hub_download( repo_id=\"rajtiwariee/lumitrace\", filename=\"model.pth\" ) ``` **Option 2: From Training** ```bash # Use local checkpoint after training ./scripts/train.sh 1 configs/lol_v1_temporal.yml # Stage 1 ./scripts/train.sh 2 configs/lol_v1_temporal.yml # Stage 2 ``` ### Enhance Videos ```bash # Enhance a video (auto-detects best model) ./scripts/enhance_video.sh input.mp4 output.mp4 # With specific checkpoint ./scripts/enhance_video.sh input.mp4 output.mp4 checkpoints/lol_v1/stage2/best.pth ``` ### Generate Comparisons ```bash # Create side-by-side comparison images python scripts/generate_comparisons.py \\ --checkpoint checkpoints/lol_v1/stage2/best.pth \\ --count 10 ``` ## \ud83d\udcd6 Training ### Download Datasets ```bash ./scripts/download_data.sh ``` This downloads: - LOL-v1 (500MB) - LOL-v2-Real (2.5GB) - Pretrained RetinexFormer weights ### Train Your Own Model ```bash # Stage 1: Train temporal modules (frozen backbone) ./scripts/train.sh 1 configs/lol_v1_temporal.yml # Stage 2: Fine-tune all parameters ./scripts/train.sh 2 configs/lol_v1_temporal.yml # Train on LOL-v2-Real ./scripts/train.sh 1 configs/lol_v2_real_temporal.yml ./scrip"
